    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The stack is a data structure in which the element added at last will be removed first. Stack follows the LIFO (Last In First Out) principle."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Think of the stack data structure as a pile of plates one on the top of another. You can only add a new plate on top of the stack or remove the top plate from the stack."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The STL stack provides the functionality of a stack data structure in C++."
    },
